ul.li:
fetches a GDK-Proton built from a WineGDK fork that implements XUser
          and request signing, so you sign in to Microsoft inside the game —
          no relay, no proxy;

removes thin top and left borders from WineX11 fullscreen
              rendering and restores touchpad or mouse-wheel scrolling
              throughout the settings tabs;

keeps newly created isolated profiles beside the active managed
              profile without changing direct BOL_HOME
              data-root overrides;

keeps Flatpak's private data directory writable while
              migrating the previous data root read-only, fixing startup on
              Bazzite, CachyOS and other Flatpak hosts;

loads Minecraft's Windows Achievements catalog with a
              dedicated user-only XSTS token while preserving the packaged
              Windows title, SCID and platform;

repairs an invalid managed-prefix user32.dll before
              launch and keeps the engine on its pure-WoW64 path for minimal
              Linux distributions;

adds same-tag game-build refresh, LAN diagnostics and actionable
              guidance for discovery, version mismatches and full-world errors,
              without requiring environment variables;

adds graphical GPU-crash acknowledgement, safer renderer
              diagnostics, automatic cleanup of completed launch markers and a
              guarded legacy compatibility renderer;

implements single and multiple selection for the WinAppSDK
              FileOpenPicker contract in both Wine PE architectures so world
              and skin imports no longer crash;

records normal wrapper completion before Wine teardown so a
              delayed clean shutdown cannot become a permanent GPU block, while
              interrupted and legacy sessions remain fail-closed;

ships one reviewed vkd3d-proton 3.0.1 build containing both
              device-generated-command paths: EXT DGC on current drivers and
              the restored NV DGC fallback on older NVIDIA drivers;

blocks degraded FBDEV/software X11 sessions and recent fatal GPU
              kernel faults before Wine or Vulkan starts, preventing a broken
              host driver from turning PLAY into a full-system hard lock;

records each GPU launch durably, checks the previous kernel boot,
              and refuses a blind retry after a power-loss interruption until
              the repaired incident is explicitly acknowledged;

writes WineGDK/GameInput registry values offline and atomically,
              eliminating the pre-game UMU/Explorer processes; isolates the
              managed prefix and disables automatic kill/relaunch loops;

fixes the 1.2.9 engine updater incorrectly treating the managed
              WineGDK engine as a custom engine, and makes engine replacement
              validated and transactional;

with "Advanced diagnostics" enabled the game could hang or crash
              with broken menus — the verbose logging was flooding and starving
              the game; it now stays fast and playable with diagnostics on;

the game no longer freezes on the "Get Started" screen with the
              music still playing — the online-login component it needs is now
              published, so signing in completes instead of hanging;

fixes the crash when opening or closing Settings or pausing the
              game (seen mainly on the Steam Deck) by giving the game more
              stack room;

redesigned launcher with rounded, flat controls and crisp
              antialiased text — and it is fully self-contained, so it looks
              the same on every distribution with nothing to install;

fixes a crash on the first launch after install, caused by
              Proton's OpenXR runtime — VR is now fully disabled so the game
              starts straight into normal (flat) mode;

initialises the Wine prefix before installing the input and
              login components, fixing a "system32 not found" failure on a
              fresh install;
